{"kind":"artifact","text":"The layer contract states the property for the citation guard, and the mechanism only where a mechanism is what is guaranteed. Exact clean pushed head 2dd9f72da31912fc501ee4bb7b108d6048bee58c on request/repo-remote-link; tree 15594a41, checkout clean, origin matching. Under planner's repair child 59c1ab8d and my promise 5e4e6fc4.\n\nWHAT CHANGED AND WHY THIS SHAPE. The sentence I wrote earlier in this lane claimed the same sanitising covers the pathspec variables so the guard cannot be silenced into finding nothing. Codex proved the head did not keep that contract, and planner ruled on the direction: state the property, not the mechanism.\n\nThe page now says the guard refuses whenever it cannot positively confirm that no live document cites the target, and that a lookup which does not run at all — a broken Git, a resource limit, a hostile command-scope configuration — yields a refusal and never a silent pass. It says in as many words that bounding the environment narrows how such a lookup is reached, is not what makes the answer safe, and that no list of variable names is load-bearing.\n\nWHY THAT IS THE RIGHT DISTINCTION AND NOT JUST SOFTER WORDING. A claim about a list of stripped variables is a claim about what its author thought of. Mine was wrong within a day, in this same lane, in a way codex found in minutes. A claim about an outcome stays true when a variable nobody anticipated gets through, which is the only kind of claim a security contract can afford to make about an open-ended input space.\n\nWHAT DELIBERATELY REMAINS A MECHANISM CLAIM. The remote read is still described as bounded by both the local configuration scope and a sanitised routing environment, because there the mechanism is the guarantee: there is no outcome to state instead, and both bounds are separately necessary. The two halves of this paragraph make different kinds of promise on purpose.\n\nGATES, run by me at this exact head from a run I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached. npm test 131 pass, 0 fail. gofmt empty; build, vet and diff-check exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"2dd9f72da31912fc501ee4bb7b108d6048bee58c","path":"docs/reference/architecture.md"}}